this is an extension of #9267 for 1:1 association
### What you did

``` php
class UsersController extends AppController
{
    public function profile()
    {
        $user = $this->Users->get($this->Auth->user('id'), [
            'contain' => ['Profiles']
        ]);
        if ($this->request->is(['patch', 'post', 'put'])) {
            $user = $this->Users->patchEntity($user, $this->request->data);
            if ($this->Users->save($user)) {
                $this->Flash->success(__("Yay"));
            } else {
                $this->Flash->error(__("Derp"));
            }
        }
        $this->set(compact('user'));
    }
}
```

``` php
class UsersTable extends Table
{
    public function initialize(array $config)
    {
        $this->hasOne('Profiles', [
            'dependent' => true
        ]);
    }
}
```

``` php
class ProfilesTable extends Table
{
    public function initialize(array $config)
    {
        $this->belongsTo('Users', [
            'foreignKey' => 'user_id',
            'joinType' => 'INNER'
        ]);
    }
}
```
### Expected Behavior

The profile entity is being updated when posting data like 

``` php
[
    'id' => 'fafde4e3-25b1-4869-94b6-1b8530e663cf',
    'profile' => [
        'firstname' => 'ADMIN',
        'lastname' => 'ISTRATOR',
        'notification' => 1
    ],
    'email' => 'new@email.com',
]
```
### Actual Behavior

The Profile entity not being updated.Its fields are mark as dirty but 'profile' is not dirty in the user entity

```
object(App\Model\Entity\User) {

        'id' => 'f6ae698f-3ce1-400f-b218-eda119718e73',
        'email' => 'new@email.com',
        'profile' => object(App\Model\Entity\Profile) {
            'id' => (int) 11,
            'user_id' => 'f6ae698f-3ce1-400f-b218-eda119718e73',
            'firstname' => 'ADMIN',
            'lastname' => 'ISTRATEUR',
            'notification' => true,
            '[new]' => false,
            '[accessible]' => [
                'user_id' => true,
                'firstname' => true,
                'lastname' => true,
                'notification' => true
            ],
            '[dirty]' => [
                'firstname' => true,
                'lastname' => true,
            ],
            '[original]' => [
                'firstname' => 'AD',
                'lastname' => 'MIN',
            ],
            '[virtual]' => [],
            '[errors]' => [],
            '[invalid]' => [],
            '[repository]' => 'Profiles'

        },
        '[new]' => false,
        '[accessible]' => [
            'profile' => true,
            'email' => true
        ],
        '[dirty]' => [
            'email' => true
        ],
        '[original]' => [
            'email' => 'admin@admin.fr'
        ],
        '[virtual]' => [],
        '[errors]' => [],
        '[invalid]' => [],
        '[repository]' => 'Users'
}
```

As you can see, `profile` is not added in as `dirty` in the `User` entity  after patching and therefore is not saved.

The previous patch did not solved this case, and I didn't found any existing test that covers this scenario.
